#%PAM-1.0
# sshd sends the password method and keyboard-interactive through this one stack, and answers each
# hidden prompt of the password method with the password. So the code comes first and a failed code
# falls through to the password: on passtotp the password step signs in and keyboard-interactive
# asks for the code. That also lets a wrong code followed by the password in on passtotp, so a
# wrong-code cell belongs on totp or keytotp. Those start with PASSWORD_ACCESS=false, which keeps
# /etc/shadow from sshd, so pam_unix always fails there and only the code signs in. pam_unix also
# reports an unreadable shadow entry as an expired account, hence pam_permit for the account check.
auth [success=done default=ignore] pam_google_authenticator.so secret=/config/.google_authenticator
auth required pam_unix.so
account required pam_permit.so
session include base-session
